From 08b0107f9b7e88c2e56096644d59d9a038bc5f96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: robin <robin800601@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 19:28:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] mm: shard file i_mmap trees by NUMA domain

Add an experimental CONFIG_NUMA_DOMAIN_I_MMAP_SHARDS mode that lazily migrates ordinary file mappings from the legacy address_space i_mmap tree to per-NUMA-domain interval trees protected by per-shard rwsems.

Preserve fork-side file VMA batching and exit-side unlink batching by grouping operations by mapping and stable mm i_mmap domain nid. Keep DAX and hugetlb mappings on the legacy tree, and teach rmap, unmap, pagewalk, khugepaged, memory-failure, and mm_take_all_locks to handle sharded roots.

The option defaults off.
---
